    "answer_2": "It helps or fails according to whether slow accepted drift really adds useful carry beyond breakout impulse and range rotation. Vs the current two-sleeve baseline it delivers dReturn +20.69pp and dMaxDD -0.06pp. In `major_drawdown` it adds dReturn -0.08pp and dMaxDD -0.06pp, but in `recovery_phase` it slips to dReturn +0.98pp even though dMaxDD stays +0.08pp. The early-recovery window is also mixed at dReturn -0.29pp and dMaxDD +0.07pp.",
